{"id": "EUVD-2026-80519", "enisaUuid": "07c9c37d-770c-3dc0-8106-6acc318b0693", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: keyop: use mmu_lock to read gmap->asce\n\nEvery other dat_* consumer in this file (kvm_s390_get_skeys,\nset_skeys, get_cmma_bits, set_cmma_bits, MEM_CLR_CMMA,\nkvm_s390_fixup_prefix, kvm_test_age_gfn, kvm_age_gfn) reads\nkvm->arch.gmap->asce *inside* the mmu_lock read-side. keyop is the only\noutlier.\n\ngmap->asce is mutated under write_lock(mmu_lock) by gmap_set_limit()\nand keyop might use a stale asce value for walking as KVM_S390_KEYOP\nand KVM_S390_VM_MEM_LIMIT_SIZE can run concurrently. This can result\nin memory corruption.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:54:53", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae452b990e0544425f77045351c56e77158858e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da07a751efa4583385f9f0f47113549fe8871242"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xrcv-f2mv-23j2", "CVE-2026-89919"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "377d2591-4231-3937-8a88-1f8a0a86c6f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4ef2de6e-a6fe-354f-94a3-bb4e9932f328", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ee4ddc1647b8b3b9e7a94d798a1774a764428c1 <da07a751efa4583385f9f0f47113549fe8871242"}, {"id": "9174c5aa-5574-361c-857b-6f5bb7d77632", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "96074dfe-26e0-3cda-a519-613ba00cfc38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b937e3c2-1a97-3896-9a38-5bce7f813bf3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0ee4ddc1647b8b3b9e7a94d798a1774a764428c1 <ae452b990e0544425